.TH FL-TASKMGR 1 "November 2026" "fldesktop 0.1.0" "fldesktop"
.SH NAME
fl-taskmgr \- task manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfl-taskmgr\fR [\fB\-\-performance\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Lists running processes with their CPU and memory use, and graphs the system load.
.SS Processes
Click a column header to sort; click it again to reverse the order. The filter box matches
names, command lines, PIDs and user names. \fBAll users\fR shows other users' processes as well,
\fBTree view\fR nests child processes under their parents, and the menu can show kernel threads.
.PP
The context menu (right-click) can end (SIGTERM) or kill (SIGKILL) a process, stop and continue it,
change its priority (nice value), open the folder of its executable and show its properties.
\fBDelete\fR ends the selected process, \fBShift+Delete\fR kills it, \fBAlt+Enter\fR shows its
properties. Signalling another user's process, or raising a priority, asks for authentication
through \fBpkexec\fR(1).
.SS Performance
Sixty seconds of history for each CPU (or all CPUs combined), memory and swap, network traffic
and disk throughput.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-performance\fR
Start on the Performance tab.
.SH KEYS
\fBCtrl+Shift+Escape\fR starts the task manager (a default \fBfl-wm\fR binding).
\fBF5\fR refreshes, \fBCtrl+Q\fR quits.
.SH FILES
.TP
\fI~/.config/fldesktop/taskmgr.ini\fR
Update interval, sort column, tree view and the other view settings.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBfl-wm\fR(1), \fBkill\fR(1), \fBrenice\fR(1), \fBproc\fR(5)
